= Ernst Meyer

Meyer is a former chairman of the party and its mediator. He is a follower of Levi's mass-politics course without having left with Levi, and he is trusted by neither extreme.

- @mediate
- @mass_party
- @root: Return to main

@mediate
title: Mediate between the factions
subtitle: Calm the quarrels between the factions. · dev: kf_right_dissent −3, kf_left_dissent −3, kf_centre_dissent −3
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before next advisor action. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 4; kf_right_dissent -= 3; kf_left_dissent -= 3; kf_centre_dissent -= 3

Meyer brings the factions to the table and drafts a compromise that none of them likes, and all can live with. The calm will not last unless something changes.

@mass_party
title: Argue for the mass party
subtitle: Make the case for a long, patient course. · dev: kf_centre_strength +5, kf_left_dissent +2
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before next advisor action. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 4; kf_centre_strength += 5; kf_left_dissent += 2

Meyer argues that a party of a few hundred thousand cannot make a revolution alone. The Left calls it a retreat; the members who have seen the March Action are less sure.
